{number: 35}
{title: Low In The Grave He Lay}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Low in the grave He lay, [F] Jesus my [C] Savior!
[C] Waiting the coming day, [Am] Jesus my [G7] Lord!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Up from the [C] grave He a-[G] rose,
With a [F] mighty triumph [G7] o'er His [C] foes;
He a-[G] rose a Victor from the [C] dark domain,
And He [F] lives for-[Dm] ever with His [G] saints to reign:
He a-[C] rose! He a-[F] rose!
Halle-[C] lujah! [G7] Christ a-[C] rose!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Vainly they watch His bed, [F] Jesus my [C] Savior!
[C] Vainly they seal the dead, [Am] Jesus my [G7] Lord!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Death cannot keep his prey, [F] Jesus my [C] Savior!
[C] He tore the bars away, [Am] Jesus my [G7] Lord!
{end_of_verse}
